EU Seller Operations, Finance, Tax Counsel,

VAT RETURN PERIOD 10/2026 - DEFERRED
FILING WINDOW.
Registration 455-312-889 (non-established
taxable person, Amazon EU marketplace
fulfiled) has a deferred filing window
for period 10/2026 pending reconciliation
of marketplace-collected VAT. The window
closes on the 7th of next month.

1. PERIOD SUMMARY

  VAT registration:   455-312-889
                      (NETP, goods)
  Period:             10/2026
                      (1 Oct - 31 Oct 2026)
  Scheme:             Marketplace
                      collection (import
                      B2C < GBP 135) +
                      seller-declared
                      UK stock
  Marketplace VAT
    collected:        GBP 21,447.92
  Seller-declared
    output tax:       GBP 8,912.40
  Discrepancy under
    review:           GBP 1,204.15
                      ("FBA multichannel"
                      line unmatched)
  Filing reference:   VAT907-455-312-889-
                      1026

2. HOW TO FILE (OFFICIAL PATH ONLY)

    1. Type the Government Gateway
       address yourself
       (tax.service.gov.uk style -
       use the address from your
       registration certificate,
       not from any email).
    2. Sign in with your Gateway
       user ID and password.
    3. Submit the VAT return for
       period 10/2026 and upload
       supporting records
       (marketplace reports, C79s)
       through the same session.

  HMRC will NEVER:
  - Email a "deferred filing
    submission" button or link
    bound to a filing reference
  - Accept records through
    lookalike domains such as
    "hmrc-gov-uk" or
    "uk-vat-filing"
  - Offer an "agent bulk lane"
    that uploads multi-client
    reconciliations without
    per-client Gateway login
    (fiscal representatives file
    through their own Agent
    Services account)
  - Ask for marketplace sales
    ledgers, fulfilment records,
    or import evidence by email
    or reference-bound web pages

3. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - Your deferral letter (posted
    copy) carries the same
    reference VAT907-455-312-889-
    1026; compare against the
    letter, not the email
  - Sign in to the Gateway and
    check the outstanding return
    under registration
    455-312-889
  - Your fiscal representative
    receives the same schedule
    through Agent Services

4. ABOUT PENALTIES

  Penalty and surcharge positions
  are assessed and appealed
  through the Gateway
  (proof-of-posting and
  reasonable-excuse routes
  exist); an email threatening
  "automated penalty assessment
  plus marketplace joint-
  liability flagging" to force
  a web upload is not an HMRC
  process.

